{"id": "EUVD-2026-107254", "enisaUuid": "13972bd0-104d-347a-b704-8ba7633bc50c", "description": "Replaying GSS-TSIG signed UDP messages can result in memory corruption in \"`named`\".  An attacker who can capture a previously signed UDP message can replay it while the negotiated TSIG key is still valid. By also sending crafted queries to a zone the attacker controls, the attacker may potentially achieve remote code execution.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.29, 9.21.0 through 9.21.26, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.29-S1.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:45:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T23:04:30", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://kb.isc.org/docs/cve-2026-94300", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.20.30", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.21.27"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3g58-6x5w-h3fm", "CVE-2026-94300"], "assigner": "isc", "epss": 0.73, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14abee4e-1cdf-30c9-81d0-7b8384def771", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.0 \u22649.18.50"}, {"id": "3582eef7-2571-3210-84e9-f83fa1718390", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.3-S1 \u22649.18.50-S1"}, {"id": "4050b812-3330-3fd4-9dbf-f08ea1554b31", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.21.0 \u22649.21.26"}, {"id": "6c4d6e96-df79-3e9e-a0c2-45a538216bd6", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.0 \u22649.20.29"}, {"id": "9f25854d-8921-3d57-a571-353f391ab662", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.9-S1 \u22649.20.29-S1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9402bcc9-c2de-36b5-ad05-5ff18b5b1868", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}], "isExploited": false}